WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
STAR TREK

2
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
STRANGE

3
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
NEW

4
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
WＯRLDS

5
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
SEASON 01  #  EPISODE 09
"All Those Who Wander"

6
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.870
<i>Previously. on </i>STAR TREK STRANGE NEW WORLDS<i>...</i>

7
00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:29.490
HEMMER: The Aenar believe the end only comes...

8
00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:31.170
once you have fulfilled your purpose.

9
00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:33.760
It provides meaning.
- So. what was your purpose?

10
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.300
To fix what is broken.

11
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.600
What do you feel is the purpose of your life's path?

12
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.260
I really don't know.

13
00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.630
I apologize...

14
00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.890
<i>for the incident on the bridge...</i>

15
00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:44.220
<i>between Nurse Chapel and I.</i>

16
00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.220
I never actually believed you could have feelings...

17
00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:47.480
<i>for Nurse Chapel.</i>

18
00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.770
LA'AN: <i>The Gorn captured my family's colony ship.</i>

19
00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:51.940
<i>When they hunt. they're unrelenting.</i>

20
00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.230
<i>Plenty of people have seen the Gorn.</i>

21
00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:56.280
<i>They just don't live long enough to talk about it.</i>

22
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:04.280
UHURA: <i>Cadet's Personal Log. Stardate 2510.6.</i>

23
00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.830
<i>My assignment to</i> Enterprise <i>is over.</i>

24
00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:09.290
<i>After we complete our current mission...</i>

25
00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:12.580
<i>delivering vidium power cells to Deep Space Station K-7...</i>

26
00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:14.300
<i>I go back to Earth.</i>

27
00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:17.300
<i>I'm excited to see my grandmother.</i>

28
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:19.090
<i>Our last call was cut short.</i>

29
00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:21.930
<i>Life on a starship has a way of taking over.</i>

30
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.310
<i>I've rotated through almost every department.</i>

31
00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:28.930
<i>So many amazing. talented people.</i>

32
00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:31.400
<i>The top everyone of everything.</i>

33
00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:35.020
<i>They all know why they belong in Starfleet.</i>

34
00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:38.780
<i>For them. Starfleet has always been the destination.</i>

35
00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:40.570
<i>For me...</i>

36
00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:43.030
<i>it was where I ran to after the loss of my parents.</i>

37
00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:46.200
<i>Serving aboard</i> Enterprise <i>is an affirmation...</i>

38
00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.370
<i>of this entire crew's hopes and dreams.</i>

39
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.630
<i>I envy their surety.</i>

40
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.600
<i>But...</i>

41
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:54.550
<i>me...</i>

42
00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:57.260
<i>I guess I'm still searching.</i>

43
00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:59.460
PIKE: Time to bend some ears.

44
00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.130
Welcome to the big send-off.

45
00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:04.080
Although they leave us in a couple of weeks. today it's official.

46
00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:06.510
Let's hear it for Cadets Chia and Uhura for completing...

47
00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.640
their training rotation on the <i>U.S.S. Enterprise.</i>

48
00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:10.310
[APPLAUSE]

49
00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.860
You have both been exemplary crew members.

50
00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:23.240
Dedicated.

51
00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:24.290
Hardworking.

52
00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:25.710
Collaborative.

53
00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:28.000
We've seen some things together.
- MAN: Yeah. we have.

54
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.750
[LAUGHTER]
- We've survived some things together.

55
00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.370
[SCATTERED CHUCKLING]
- Hmm.

56
00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:33.670
We are bonded now and forever...

57
00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:35.250
by the family that is Starfleet.

58
00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:39.510
And speaking of bonds and oaths...

59
00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:42.850
Ensign Duke. front and center.

60
00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.930
Effective immediately. you are no longer an Ensign.

61
00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:52.060
Congratulations. Lieutenant Duke.

62
00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:53.610
[LAUGHTER. APPLAUSE]

63
00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:54.690
[LAUGHS]

64
00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:58.320
[QUIET CHATTER]

65
00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:08.950
All this time on the ship. and you still shy away from the crowd?

66
00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:10.580
Permission to speak freely. sir?

67
00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:12.580
Nyota. it's me.

68
00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:14.830
Live it up. it's a party.

69
00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.090
It's your party.

70
00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:20.430
Yes. permission granted.

71
00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:22.930
I hate goodbyes.

72
00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.220
Still haven't decided to stay?

73
00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:30.140
I know better than to beat a dead horse...

74
00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.650
but you've made an impact here.

75
00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:36.110
There will always a place on <i>Enterprise</i> for Nyota Uhura.

76
00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:38.490
[COMMS CHIRPING]
- SPOCK: <i>Spock to Captain Pike.</i>

77
00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:45.120
What is it. Spock?

78
00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.400
<i>Incoming priority 1 mission from Starfleet Command. sir.</i>

79
00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:49.150
<i>Spock out.</i>
- [COMMS CHIRPING]

80
00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.580
Aren't we already a priority 1 mission?

81
00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:53.630
Yeah.

82
00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:57.170
Where's La'An?
- She couldn't make it. She's...

83
00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:59.720
scheduled personal health time.

84
00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:01.760
She can join us in progress.

85
00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:02.800
Get Science and Medical.

86
00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:09.640
They need to send someone else.

87
00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.890
It's not someone else's assignment.

88
00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:16.070
Sorry I'm late. I was with Dr. Sanchez again.

89
00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:17.860
Head shrinker.

90
00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.650
It's called Starfleet Recovery Assistance...

91
00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.110
and I'm glad you're making use of it.

92
00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:22.490
You're on time. We're just kicking around...

93
00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:23.780
some intel on a mission brief.

94
00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.370
While you clean up?

95
00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:27.660
People are capable of doing 2 things at once.

96
00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.750
Spock?
- Approximately 4 days ago...

97
00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:32.000
the <i>U.S.S. Peregrine</i> activated a distress beacon...

98
00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.080
before losing contact.

99
00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.340
Can you take over the dishes for a minute?

100
00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.510
Oh. Yes. of course.

101
00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:42.760
Saved you a plate.
- No. thanks. I'm not hungry.

102
00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.470
You're gonna want to try the omelet and the bacon.

103
00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:45.640
And the waffle.

104
00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:47.680
PIKE: The <i>Peregrine's</i> deep space relay...

105
00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.520
took 2 days to reach Starfleet.

106
00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:54.190
Another 2 to us. so we might still have contact. just delayed.

107
00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:56.320
Oh. my God. this is delicious.
- Told you.

108
00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:58.900
At the time of transmission. the <i>Peregrine</i> was making...

109
00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.650
an unscheduled emergency landing on a Class-L planet.

110
00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:03.070
Valeo Beta V.

111
00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:05.240
Are emergency landings ever scheduled?

112
00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.410
The ship made its descent...

113
00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.240
but its beacon went out mid-transmission.

114
00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:11.790
Destroyed on impact? Where... Uh. do you have the... Where's the...

115
00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:12.830
Extra cheese?
- Mmm.

116
00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:15.580
While possible. it is more likely...

117
00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:18.710
the interference on Valeo Beta V has disrupted the signal.

118
00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:21.170
The upper atmosphere is littered with charged nitrate ions.

119
00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:22.720
UNA: Planet's a known dead zone.

120
00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:25.180
Our communications and transporters don't reach the surface.

121
00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:27.720
A <i>Sombra-class</i> ship. that's unique.

122
00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.520
I served on one. Fast.

123
00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.310
Built with the same parts as a <i>Constitution.</i>

124
00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:35.980
She'd gone off the grid. gathering data in uncharted sectors.

125
00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:39.360
The Federation wants us to aid the crew and. if possible...

126
00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:40.610
retrieve the ship.

127
00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:41.610
And our current mission?

128
00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.410
The vidium power cells for K-7.

129
00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.370
Without them the whole space station goes dark.

130
00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:47.870
Including life support.

131
00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:49.410
The nearest ship that could deliver them for us...

132
00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:50.580
is a week away.

133
00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:52.250
SPOCK: Vidium cells decay in transport.

134
00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:54.670
A delay of that duration would render them all useless.

135
00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:56.340
I advise we send a landing party...

136
00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.210
to make repairs and treat the wounded.

137
00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:02.130
Meanwhile. <i>Enterprise</i> can continue on to deliver the vidium.

138
00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:03.510
Like you said. sir.

139
00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:06.260
People are capable of doing 2 things at once.

140
00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:08.600
Let me get you some bacon.

141
00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:09.850
It's risky.

142
00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:12.270
There's no way the landing party could contact the ship.

143
00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:15.480
True. it is a communications dead zone...

144
00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:17.770
but I have faith in our crew to get it done.

145
00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:20.070
The <i>Enterprise</i> can pick us up on the way back.

146
00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:22.150
Us?
- PIKE: I'll oversee this one personally.

147
00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:24.110
Get the cadets out on 1 last away mission...

148
00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:25.120
with Senior Officers.

149
00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:27.280
You sure you want to split up the crew?

150
00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:28.870
It'll be fine. Number One.

151
00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:30.290
You get the supplies to K-7...

152
00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:33.400
I'll pile the kids in the station wagon. take a road trip.

153
00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:35.460
Sir? The station wagon?

154
00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:38.380
Anybody has to go. now's the time.

155
00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:40.050
Do not make me turn this car around.

156
00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:45.470
Okay. You have your orders.

157
00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:50.850
[OVER COMMS] <i>Number One. you're good to go.</i>

158
00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:52.180
<i>We're making our descent now.</i>

159
00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:53.520
UNA: <i>We'll monitor your approach.</i>

160
00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:55.860
PIKE: <i>That's a negative. Once we enter the upper atmosphere</i>...

161
00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:58.110
<i>we're going to be out of contact...</i>

162
00:06:58.110 --> 00:06:59.320
[DISTORTED] <i>Make haste to K-7.</i>

163
00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:12.120
[THUNDER RUMBLING]

164
00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.300
[WIND WHISTLING]

165
00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:29.520
[THUNDER RUMBLING]

166
00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.600
Man. this is gonna be a hike.

167
00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:35.690
Geothermal anomalies have forced us to land...

168
00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:37.190
several kilometers from the <i>Peregrine.</i>

169
00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:39.820
We should work quickly. This area is highly volatile.

170
00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:41.280
It is due to be overrun by an ice storm...

171
00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:42.570
in approximately 6 hours.

172
00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:43.860
This wind...

173
00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:46.780
reminds me of Andoria.

174
00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:48.080
[LAUGHS]
- [EXHALES]

175
00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:49.660
Glad someone can enjoy it.

176
00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:53.370
The anomalies. is that what's killing our comms?

177
00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:54.620
Negative. Ensign.

178
00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:55.830
It is the ionic interference...

179
00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:57.590
that prevents long-range communication.

180
00:07:57.590 --> 00:07:59.710
Drink. You owe him a drink. Spock.

181
00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:03.840
Duke's a Lieutenant now.

182
00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:06.260
Call him an Ensign. you got to buy him a drink.

183
00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:07.350
Starfleet tradition.

184
00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:10.310
Another human drinking game.

185
00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:12.730
Does their number have no limit?

186
00:08:12.730 --> 00:08:13.730
Nope.

187
00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:19.070
M'BENGA: Based on these readings...

188
00:08:19.070 --> 00:08:21.940
the <i>Peregrine</i> made landfall near the ridge of a great chasm.

189
00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:23.910
No life signs. anything?

190
00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:25.570
[TRICORDER BEEPING]

191
00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:29.160
Still too much interference.

192
00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:31.450
PIKE: We should be getting something.

193
00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:32.710
LA'AN: Captain.

194
00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:34.580
Might not be a scanning problem.

195
00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:53.090
STAR TREK

196
00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:53.090
STRANGE

197
00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:53.090
NEW

198
00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:53.090
WＯRLDS

199
00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:53.090
SEASON 01  #  EPISODE 09
"All Those Who Wander"

200
00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:44.970
PIKE: Space.

201
00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:48.540
The final frontier.

202
00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:54.110
These are the voyages of the starship Enterprise.

203
00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:57.850
Its 5-year mission...

204
00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:01.260
to explore strange new worlds...

205
00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:05.480
to seek out new life...

206
00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:08.450
and new civilizations...

207
00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:11.920
to boldly go...

208
00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:13.750
where no one has gone before.

209
00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:16.250
[ ♪ THEME MUSIC ♪ ]

210
00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:18.300
♪♪

211
00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:48.500
♪♪

212
00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:16.660
♪♪

213
00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:30.740
[STATIC]

214
00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:37.750
[CLANGS]

215
00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:40.460
[WIND WHISTLING]

216
00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:42.130
[METAL GROANING]

217
00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:08.450
Blood.

218
00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:13.700
SPOCK: Captain. there's more blood over here as well.

219
00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:17.750
I want a full diagnostic. As fast as you can.

220
00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:25.430
Any luck on the internal comms?

221
00:11:25.430 --> 00:11:27.550
No. Still down.

222
00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:29.890
And environmental systems are at 20%.

223
00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:32.520
Captain. the bridge is completely offline.

224
00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:34.720
Someone hardwired all the controls down to Engineering.

225
00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:36.560
Why would they do that?

226
00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:38.270
HEMMER: Plasma in the main circuits.

227
00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:39.360
That's not typical.

228
00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:42.110
They were likely using energy from the warp core injectors...

229
00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:43.280
as emergency power.

230
00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:44.490
But that would imply...

231
00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:45.780
UHURA: No backup batteries.

232
00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:48.240
And the matter-antimatter reactor's busted.

233
00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:50.410
Clearly I brought the right people for the job.

234
00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:52.450
Hem. can you fix it?
- Perhaps.

235
00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:54.540
I'll have to work in Engineering.

236
00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:58.380
Mr. Spock. can you manage restoring bridge functions?

237
00:11:58.380 --> 00:11:59.840
I will attempt to make quick work of it.

238
00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:01.000
[CLATTERING]

239
00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:08.510
It's grim.

240
00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:12.220
20 casualties so far. 1 of them the Captain.

241
00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:18.100
The <i>Peregrine</i> has a crew of 99.

242
00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:19.690
There could be more we didn't find.

243
00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:22.030
Most died of hypothermia.

244
00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:25.650
Their suits are shredded by the elements.

245
00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:28.120
Some of them were picked apart. maybe...

246
00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:30.330
local wildlife.

247
00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:32.830
Maybe something else.

248
00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:34.830
As far as I can tell...

249
00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:37.830
the crew went outside. got caught in a brutal storm...

250
00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:40.880
and couldn't find their way back to the ship.

251
00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:42.550
Pull up the logs.

252
00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:49.260
I bet it's real creepy here after dark.

253
00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:52.310
It's already pretty damn creepy.

254
00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:56.520
CHIA: Lieutenant Kirk. We found something.

255
00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:05.400
What the hell did this?

256
00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:20.000
I can only get audio.

257
00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:24.510
GAVIN: <i>Captain's Log. Stardate...</i>

258
00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:26.050
<i>I'm not even sure.</i>

259
00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:27.720
<i>A week since we've crashed?</i>

260
00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:30.680
Peregrine <i>was mapping non-Federation space...</i>

261
00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:33.810
<i>when we found 3 castaways on an M-Class planet.</i>

262
00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:37.190
<i>A human girl. a humanoid of unknown origin...</i>

263
00:13:37.190 --> 00:13:39.560
<i>and an Orion named Pasko.</i>

264
00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:41.980
<i>We rescued them. Brought them aboard.</i>

265
00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:44.690
<i>But we didn't know what we didn't know.</i>

266
00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:47.900
<i>Pasko was infected with Gorn eggs.</i>

267
00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:50.030
<i>Biofilters didn't detect them.</i>

268
00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:51.410
<i>But the Orion knew.</i>

269
00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:54.080
<i>He set off a plasma grenade in Engineering...</i>

270
00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:55.250
<i>tried to end it.</i>

271
00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:57.250
<i>The system sent an automatic distress call...</i>

272
00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:58.790
<i>in response to the explosion.</i>

273
00:13:59.590 --> 00:14:02.710
<i>If I could reach Starfleet now. I would say</i>

274
00:14:02.710 --> 00:14:05.050
<i>"Stay away."</i>

275
00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:08.050
<i>"Don't come to Valeo Beta V."</i>

276
00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:09.800
A little late for that. isn't it?

277
00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:11.810
M'Benga. Spock. go get the others.

278
00:14:12.640 --> 00:14:14.120
GAVIN: <i>But if you're watching this...</i>

279
00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:17.270
<i>chances are we didn't survive.</i>

280
00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:20.610
La'An.

281
00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:24.030
What do you want to do?
- I want to kill them.

282
00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:28.240
But I'd settle for finding any crew alive...

283
00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:30.240
and getting off of this frozen rock.

284
00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:32.790
Captain. ops are coming online.

285
00:14:32.790 --> 00:14:35.160
I have 2 life signs on Deck 5.

286
00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:36.160
Human or Gorn?

287
00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:37.920
UHURA: 1 human...

288
00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:40.340
the other...

289
00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:43.420
unknown.

290
00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:47.380
Hemmer...

291
00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:49.340
keep powering up whatever you can.

292
00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:51.390
And. La'An. Uhura. you're with me.

293
00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:52.720
[WEAPON POWERING UP]

294
00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:22.550
This body's been badly mangled.

295
00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:47.240
[CLATTERING]

296
00:15:56.910 --> 00:15:58.580
[WEAPON POWERS UP]

297
00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:01.130
[GROWLS]

298
00:16:01.130 --> 00:16:02.880
<i>Kakalaka jarfuk pikarak!</i>

299
00:16:03.340 --> 00:16:04.420
[GROWLS]

300
00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:05.550
PIKE: What's he saying?

301
00:16:05.550 --> 00:16:07.720
Universal translator isn't processing it.

302
00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:09.180
Uhura. do something.

303
00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:10.840
That's not how linguistics works.

304
00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:13.100
<i>Karfuk. Karfick. Karfarsh.</i>

305
00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:15.480
Wait.

306
00:16:16.480 --> 00:16:18.100
It's 2 life signs. right?

307
00:16:19.150 --> 00:16:21.190
<i>Shipa. Shipa.</i>

308
00:16:21.190 --> 00:16:22.980
UHURA: He might be protecting someone.

309
00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:24.570
We should lower our weapons.

310
00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:29.200
[WEAPON POWERS DOWN]

311
00:16:30.410 --> 00:16:31.410
Stand down.

312
00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:37.210
[GROWLS SOFTLY]

313
00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:41.130
I hope you're right about this.

314
00:16:41.130 --> 00:16:42.130
[WEAPON POWERS DOWN]

315
00:16:44.380 --> 00:16:45.380
UHURA: We're friends.

316
00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:47.760
We're here to help you.

317
00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:51.720
And whoever might be with you.

318
00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:54.680
[GROWLS SOFTLY]

319
00:17:08.900 --> 00:17:10.940
♪♪

320
00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:21.790
[GRUNTS SOFTLY]

321
00:17:33.310 --> 00:17:34.390
SPOCK: <i>Nurse Chapel...</i>

322
00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:36.350
I need dermal synthesizers for a burn wound.

323
00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:39.850
Where? You look fine.

324
00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:41.440
Lieutenant Duke.

325
00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:44.480
He did not account for potential instabilities...

326
00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:45.480
in the Jefferies tube.

327
00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:47.990
Duke wasn't paying attention.

328
00:17:47.990 --> 00:17:49.150
Indeed.

329
00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:51.860
Although I do fail to see the logic in asking me...

330
00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:53.990
to come for supplies instead of seeking treatment.

331
00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:55.330
Mmm. well...

332
00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:56.830
Duke made rank. Spock.

333
00:17:57.580 --> 00:17:59.080
He's acting tough.

334
00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:01.460
Pride. A flawed human emotion.

335
00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:03.000
It's called foolish for a reason.

336
00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:06.170
Thankfully. the teachings of Surak allow me to purge such things.

337
00:18:06.170 --> 00:18:07.800
One does not take pride in logic.

338
00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:13.010
I understand that. uh. Vulcans have a strong. hidden primal nature.

339
00:18:13.890 --> 00:18:16.020
I bet you're a tempest when you're angry.

340
00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:18.140
It is true that without proper mindfulness

341
00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:20.270
Vulcan emotion is dangerous.

342
00:18:20.270 --> 00:18:21.860
We use logic to not succumb to anger.

343
00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:25.480
It's good to get mad sometimes.

344
00:18:27.440 --> 00:18:29.820
UHURA: I'm gonna miss you. Hemmer.
- HEMMER: Nonsense.

345
00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:32.030
People tend to find their way back around in Starfleet.

346
00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:34.160
Mmm... Not me.

347
00:18:36.040 --> 00:18:37.870
When you asked me about my life path...

348
00:18:37.870 --> 00:18:40.170
I didn't have an answer.

349
00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:43.840
So I had to ask myself...

350
00:18:44.590 --> 00:18:47.550
"Uhura. why don't you have an answer?"

351
00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:50.180
And what was Uhura's response?

352
00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:54.350
I've just been drifting.

353
00:18:54.350 --> 00:18:56.100
It's time for me to stop coasting.

354
00:18:56.100 --> 00:18:59.440
And you feel that serving with Starfleet is coasting?

355
00:18:59.770 --> 00:19:02.150
[CHUCKLE SOFTLY] I don't know.

356
00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:04.070
Maybe.

357
00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:06.780
Who knows where I'll end up.

358
00:19:07.860 --> 00:19:09.070
But...

359
00:19:09.070 --> 00:19:10.950
I'm not afraid to face it alone anymore.

360
00:19:11.740 --> 00:19:12.740
Interesting.

361
00:19:13.660 --> 00:19:15.830
I never felt that your fear was being alone.

362
00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:18.170
I think your problem is the exact opposite.

363
00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:21.750
Oh. really? Please. enlighten me.

364
00:19:21.750 --> 00:19:23.920
You make friends easily. when you allow it to happen.

365
00:19:25.960 --> 00:19:27.800
You think I don't like making friends?

366
00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:30.680
No. I think you love it.

367
00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:33.970
And deep down. that scares you. 'cause...

368
00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:37.310
your real fear is putting down roots.

369
00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:39.940
So now you're a Ship's Counselor?

370
00:19:39.940 --> 00:19:42.100
[SCOFFS] I understand.

371
00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:44.690
It is better to leave than to be the one left behind.

372
00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:46.610
But that's wrong.

373
00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:49.950
You create bonds. It's a gift.

374
00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:53.700
Of course the people you care about are going to cause you pain...

375
00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:54.780
it will hurt...

376
00:19:54.780 --> 00:19:57.700
but the love it yields will far outweigh the sorrow.

377
00:19:59.830 --> 00:20:02.000
Now. hand me the electron coupler.

378
00:20:04.130 --> 00:20:06.300
<i>Piti titi camu.</i>

379
00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:09.130
<i>Topa karfarsh. Piki shipa topa.</i>

380
00:20:10.590 --> 00:20:11.590
M'BENGA: Your friend...

381
00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:13.800
what's his name?

382
00:20:14.430 --> 00:20:15.680
I call him Buckley.

383
00:20:16.350 --> 00:20:17.770
I like it.

384
00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:18.930
It's just what I call him.

385
00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:22.440
What's your name?
- Oriana.

386
00:20:24.310 --> 00:20:25.570
Are we getting out of here?

387
00:20:28.070 --> 00:20:29.530
Are you checking them thoroughly?

388
00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:32.490
Readings don't show any anomalies.

389
00:20:37.410 --> 00:20:39.000
Are you infected?

390
00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:40.290
Is he?

391
00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:41.870
I told you the readings are clean.

392
00:20:41.880 --> 00:20:43.830
Where are the Gorn?
<i>- Karfika kafk!</i>

393
00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:45.670
It's okay. Buckley. I got this.

394
00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:49.970
The monsters are gone.

395
00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:52.050
Why didn't you tell the Captain about the Gorn eggs...

396
00:20:52.050 --> 00:20:53.050
when they saved you?

397
00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:55.550
Why did you stay quiet?

398
00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:57.680
Lieutenant.
- You could've saved them.

399
00:20:57.680 --> 00:20:59.850
La'An. stop harassing my daughter.

400
00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:06.360
My patient.

401
00:21:07.860 --> 00:21:09.070
Leave her alone.

402
00:21:09.070 --> 00:21:10.820
Find somewhere else to be useful.

403
00:21:17.870 --> 00:21:19.660
PIKE: Sensors show the ship is clean.

404
00:21:20.290 --> 00:21:22.370
Whatever happened outside seems to be the end of it.

405
00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:24.710
Reported missing 2 years ago.

406
00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:26.800
Help me understand.

407
00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:28.090
Where do the Gorn fit in?

408
00:21:28.090 --> 00:21:30.380
The girl and the 2 aliens were probably refugees...

409
00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:31.430
from a breeding planet.

410
00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:34.760
The adult Gorn only harvest their young sporadically...

411
00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:37.600
so whatever was born on this ship. they are most likely alone.

412
00:21:39.390 --> 00:21:41.060
Don't take comfort in that. Captain.

413
00:21:42.270 --> 00:21:43.750
They're equally lethal on the ground.

414
00:21:44.060 --> 00:21:45.440
It only takes 1.

415
00:21:45.440 --> 00:21:47.610
Comms are still down. but we can do a security sweep.

416
00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:50.650
If there are any still alive down here.

417
00:21:58.120 --> 00:21:59.910
A soprano sings in E minor...

418
00:22:00.870 --> 00:22:02.250
and we associate a feeling.

419
00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:06.170
But it's not really about the melody.

420
00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:10.010
Our own reflections make it emotional.

421
00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:11.840
I'm not being emotional.

422
00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:13.970
I was talking about me.

423
00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:17.810
I called the girl my daughter.

424
00:22:21.140 --> 00:22:22.310
But that girl...

425
00:22:23.150 --> 00:22:24.150
Oriana...

426
00:22:25.480 --> 00:22:27.530
she's in a place few can understand.

427
00:22:28.070 --> 00:22:30.820
Before pain twists her up inside...

428
00:22:30.820 --> 00:22:34.120
she has a chance to grow beyond it. like you.

429
00:22:34.910 --> 00:22:37.330
There's no magic button you press. You just...

430
00:22:40.370 --> 00:22:41.460
You just survive.

431
00:22:42.790 --> 00:22:45.380
She just needs someone to help her see the light.

432
00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:53.180
[WEAPON POWERS UP]

433
00:23:05.610 --> 00:23:07.280
[CLATTERING IN DISTANCE]

434
00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:20.960
[RATTLES]

435
00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:27.500
[CLATTERING CONTINUES]

436
00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:34.010
[WIND BLOWING]
- [CLATTERING]

437
00:23:34.010 --> 00:23:36.060
♪♪

438
00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:46.110
Sorry. That for Lieutenant Duke?

439
00:23:47.520 --> 00:23:49.570
Oh. I didn't realize you were so jumpy.

440
00:23:58.740 --> 00:24:00.750
[WHEEZING]

441
00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:08.880
[MUFFLED HEART BEATING]

442
00:24:09.130 --> 00:24:10.260
Elevated heart rate.

443
00:24:13.340 --> 00:24:14.510
[GROANS]

444
00:24:15.890 --> 00:24:18.430
Hello. What is this now?

445
00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:21.600
Chia. pass me that light.
- Yep.

446
00:24:43.250 --> 00:24:44.920
Chia. can you calibrate for a physical?

447
00:24:44.920 --> 00:24:47.210
Just use the readings we took on him before.

448
00:24:49.880 --> 00:24:51.920
<i>Kalaka. Pika. Kalaka.</i>
- CHAPEL: Easy.

449
00:24:51.920 --> 00:24:54.430
Just gonna run a quick simulation on your scans.

450
00:24:54.430 --> 00:24:56.100
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

451
00:25:10.360 --> 00:25:12.030
[GASPING]

452
00:25:12.120 --> 00:25:14.160
♪♪

453
00:25:38.680 --> 00:25:39.810
You all right up there?

454
00:25:41.520 --> 00:25:43.270
[CONTINUES GASPING]

455
00:25:43.270 --> 00:25:45.270
[MUFFLED RUMBLING]

456
00:25:47.730 --> 00:25:49.320
[SCREAMING]

457
00:25:50.230 --> 00:25:52.240
[GROANING]

458
00:25:53.320 --> 00:25:54.320
Nurse Chapel?

459
00:25:56.620 --> 00:25:59.540
[SCREECHES]
- [SCREAMING]

460
00:26:00.080 --> 00:26:01.500
[SCREAMING]

461
00:26:01.500 --> 00:26:03.500
[CHOKING]
- [SQUEALS]

462
00:26:12.130 --> 00:26:13.800
[SQUEALING]

463
00:26:24.690 --> 00:26:26.690
[BREATHING SHAKILY]

464
00:26:27.980 --> 00:26:30.650
[CLANGS]
- [SQUEALING]

465
00:26:34.400 --> 00:26:36.200
[GORN CLUCKING]

466
00:26:41.080 --> 00:26:42.750
[BEEPS. WHIRS]

467
00:26:50.130 --> 00:26:52.550
You were lucky. Those conduits had a full current.

468
00:26:53.420 --> 00:26:55.090
[CLATTERING NEARBY]

469
00:26:59.810 --> 00:27:00.890
M'BENGA: Be glad.

470
00:27:00.890 --> 00:27:02.390
I could be amputating.

471
00:27:03.810 --> 00:27:05.100
DUKE: Great.

472
00:27:05.100 --> 00:27:08.270
1ˢᵗ mission as a Lieutenant. and I almost lose an arm.

473
00:27:08.270 --> 00:27:11.400
Don't beat yourself up. These things happen. All right?

474
00:27:12.400 --> 00:27:14.490
Duke. perhaps if you take comfort in the fact...

475
00:27:14.490 --> 00:27:16.360
that you completed the needed repairs.

476
00:27:16.370 --> 00:27:18.030
That will shape your pride...
- [GROWLING]

477
00:27:18.030 --> 00:27:19.410
[SCREAMING]

478
00:27:19.410 --> 00:27:21.080
[GORN CHITTERING]

479
00:27:21.910 --> 00:27:23.580
PIKE: Sam. grab him. Keep him still.

480
00:27:23.580 --> 00:27:25.080
[SCREAMING]

481
00:27:25.080 --> 00:27:26.170
There's 2 of 'em.

482
00:27:26.170 --> 00:27:28.090
Hold him down. I don't want to risk hitting him.

483
00:27:28.960 --> 00:27:30.750
[SCREAMING]

484
00:27:35.550 --> 00:27:36.890
[SCREAMING STOPS]

485
00:27:38.260 --> 00:27:39.890
We need to alert the rest of the crew.

486
00:27:41.430 --> 00:27:42.480
Right now.

487
00:27:57.660 --> 00:27:58.740
[WHISPERS] Oriana?

488
00:28:02.330 --> 00:28:04.000
[BEEPS. WHIRS]

489
00:28:04.500 --> 00:28:05.500
[EXHALES]

490
00:28:06.630 --> 00:28:08.130
[MUTTERS]

491
00:28:17.220 --> 00:28:19.440
♪♪

492
00:28:38.660 --> 00:28:40.330
[BREATHING SHAKILY]

493
00:28:43.660 --> 00:28:44.670
[WHISPERS] Oriana?

494
00:29:03.890 --> 00:29:06.140
[LOUD CLATTERING]
- [GASPS] It's you.

495
00:29:06.690 --> 00:29:08.810
Oh. thank God. [SIGHS]

496
00:29:08.810 --> 00:29:09.820
They came out of him.

497
00:29:10.860 --> 00:29:12.570
I... I didn't see where...

498
00:29:15.320 --> 00:29:16.490
The girl.

499
00:29:17.200 --> 00:29:18.620
4 Gorn hatchlings.

500
00:29:19.780 --> 00:29:21.370
I count 1 dead. that leaves 3.

501
00:29:23.450 --> 00:29:25.620
They'll mature soon. and then fight for dominance.

502
00:29:25.620 --> 00:29:26.620
What do we do?

503
00:29:27.670 --> 00:29:28.710
What do we do?

504
00:29:32.590 --> 00:29:33.840
Scan for biosignatures.

505
00:29:34.590 --> 00:29:35.630
Okay.

506
00:29:43.140 --> 00:29:44.520
Still no comms.

507
00:29:44.520 --> 00:29:46.940
I've hits on our people. but nothing on the Gorn.

508
00:29:46.940 --> 00:29:48.190
Does that mean they're gone?

509
00:29:49.570 --> 00:29:52.440
I doubt it. Somehow they found a way to avoid our sensors.

510
00:29:53.940 --> 00:29:55.200
So they could be anywhere.

511
00:29:56.740 --> 00:29:57.740
Take this.

512
00:29:59.030 --> 00:30:01.370
Watch the ceilings. shoot anything that moves.

513
00:30:01.370 --> 00:30:02.370
Yeah.

514
00:30:06.670 --> 00:30:08.000
[WEAPON POWERS UP]

515
00:30:09.880 --> 00:30:11.200
LA'AN: We need to find that girl.

516
00:30:15.760 --> 00:30:17.090
This is where she was before.

517
00:30:23.100 --> 00:30:24.140
[CHAPEL WHISPERS] Oriana?

518
00:30:25.140 --> 00:30:26.190
Nothing.

519
00:30:26.730 --> 00:30:28.400
[CLATTERING IN DISTANCE]

520
00:30:42.040 --> 00:30:43.120
Nice hiding spot.

521
00:30:43.790 --> 00:30:45.120
Hey. we're here to keep you safe.

522
00:30:46.460 --> 00:30:47.630
She's already safe.

523
00:30:48.500 --> 00:30:49.590
Gorn hate the cold.

524
00:30:51.300 --> 00:30:52.820
It's why you came back here. isn't it?

525
00:30:53.380 --> 00:30:54.590
Coldest place in the ship?

526
00:30:56.720 --> 00:30:57.760
It's where I'd hide.

527
00:30:58.340 --> 00:31:01.140
ORIANA: People before you tricked them into going outside.

528
00:31:03.100 --> 00:31:04.140
But now they're back.

529
00:31:04.930 --> 00:31:06.980
We leave here. we die.

530
00:31:12.650 --> 00:31:13.690
[ECHOING] Run!

531
00:31:22.660 --> 00:31:24.870
My brother died like your friend.

532
00:31:24.870 --> 00:31:26.040
The Gorn got him.

533
00:31:26.670 --> 00:31:28.290
I know what it feels like...

534
00:31:28.290 --> 00:31:30.500
to watch them hurt the people you love.

535
00:31:30.500 --> 00:31:32.000
You feel alone.

536
00:31:32.000 --> 00:31:33.960
Nobody understands the pain.

537
00:31:35.090 --> 00:31:36.340
But look at me now.

538
00:31:37.800 --> 00:31:39.840
These people I came with...

539
00:31:39.850 --> 00:31:41.510
my job is to keep them safe.

540
00:31:42.680 --> 00:31:45.310
And this crew. I believe we can do anything...

541
00:31:46.190 --> 00:31:47.400
even defeat the Gorn.

542
00:31:48.350 --> 00:31:49.980
Oriana. trust me.

543
00:31:49.980 --> 00:31:53.150
There's surviving and then there is living.

544
00:31:57.200 --> 00:31:58.240
Come on.

545
00:31:59.780 --> 00:32:01.910
[WHIRRING]

546
00:32:04.750 --> 00:32:07.710
Now. once we hit the relay switch...

547
00:32:07.710 --> 00:32:08.960
the systems will begin to cycle...

548
00:32:08.960 --> 00:32:11.500
and then we just have to reboot navigation.

549
00:32:13.050 --> 00:32:15.050
Team Hemhura strikes again. huh?

550
00:32:15.760 --> 00:32:16.970
You may have the honor.

551
00:32:20.550 --> 00:32:22.510
[ALARM WAILS]

552
00:32:22.510 --> 00:32:24.890
[ALARM STOPS]
- [GROWLING IN DISTANCE]

553
00:32:24.890 --> 00:32:26.180
What is that?

554
00:32:26.190 --> 00:32:28.190
I don't know. [SNIFFS]

555
00:32:29.350 --> 00:32:31.060
But I smell human blood.

556
00:32:35.400 --> 00:32:37.990
Power's on. Means Hemmer's making progress.

557
00:32:37.990 --> 00:32:39.780
We stay in here. we're lizard chow.

558
00:32:39.780 --> 00:32:41.530
We got to make a run for the shuttles.

559
00:32:41.530 --> 00:32:44.410
By my calculations. the ice storm outside has just begun.

560
00:32:44.410 --> 00:32:45.750
It is not safe to leave the ship.

561
00:32:45.750 --> 00:32:47.710
It isn't safe inside the ship.

562
00:32:50.080 --> 00:32:52.380
But. hey. at least we'll all die nice and warm.

563
00:32:53.090 --> 00:32:54.840
Sam. you saw I hurt one.

564
00:32:55.260 --> 00:32:56.420
We can fight them.

565
00:32:56.420 --> 00:32:57.430
[GRUNTS IN FRUSTRATION]

566
00:32:58.050 --> 00:32:59.260
[SIGHS]

567
00:32:59.260 --> 00:33:00.640
I could give him a sedative.

568
00:33:01.430 --> 00:33:03.560
No. Sam's tougher than he looks.

569
00:33:04.350 --> 00:33:05.560
And I need everyone alert.

570
00:33:06.560 --> 00:33:08.940
Captain. the internal comms are back online.

571
00:33:10.230 --> 00:33:11.560
Open a channel. all decks.

572
00:33:13.230 --> 00:33:15.280
[ALERT WAILS. CHIMES]

573
00:33:15.280 --> 00:33:16.950
PIKE: <i>All hands. emergency protocol...</i>

574
00:33:17.660 --> 00:33:19.780
<i>regroup and rendezvous in Sickbay.</i>

575
00:33:19.780 --> 00:33:22.120
<i>Repeat. get to Sickbay and watch your 6.</i>

576
00:33:24.620 --> 00:33:26.000
[CLANGS]
- [GASPS]

577
00:33:26.500 --> 00:33:30.170
[GROWLING. CLUCKING]

578
00:33:35.800 --> 00:33:36.970
[GROWLS]

579
00:33:38.930 --> 00:33:40.180
We need to make a run for it.

580
00:33:42.470 --> 00:33:43.510
No!

581
00:33:44.430 --> 00:33:46.180
Aah!
- Hemmer!

582
00:33:46.180 --> 00:33:47.520
[GROANING]
- [SNARLS]

583
00:33:49.400 --> 00:33:50.610
[SCREECHES]

584
00:34:00.990 --> 00:34:02.700
M'BENGA: Medical Officer's analysis.

585
00:34:03.490 --> 00:34:04.540
SPOCK: Fascinating.

586
00:34:05.080 --> 00:34:07.160
The Gorn's biological makeup renders them invisible...

587
00:34:07.160 --> 00:34:08.460
to all of our sensors.

588
00:34:09.210 --> 00:34:10.830
A genetic chameleon.

589
00:34:10.830 --> 00:34:12.750
That's how I missed them inside of Buckley.

590
00:34:12.750 --> 00:34:14.920
Is there anything from his bio scan we can use?

591
00:34:14.920 --> 00:34:16.090
Something trackable?

592
00:34:16.090 --> 00:34:18.890
M'BENGA: For starters. we don't even know what kind of species he was.

593
00:34:19.510 --> 00:34:21.300
And according to this...

594
00:34:21.300 --> 00:34:23.680
the maturity cycle depends on the host.

595
00:34:23.680 --> 00:34:25.680
In the Orion. it took weeks.

596
00:34:25.680 --> 00:34:27.230
Humans. days.

597
00:34:27.640 --> 00:34:29.690
These ducts in the mouth likely expel venom.

598
00:34:30.020 --> 00:34:33.360
Yes. and it burns quite tremendously.

599
00:34:33.360 --> 00:34:35.610
No doubt a toxin meant to blind its victims.

600
00:34:35.610 --> 00:34:37.780
I was not the best target.

601
00:34:37.780 --> 00:34:39.650
Hemmer. I know you have rules about telepathy.

602
00:34:39.660 --> 00:34:41.200
Any chance they don't apply to an enemy...

603
00:34:41.200 --> 00:34:42.410
that's trying to eat us?

604
00:34:42.410 --> 00:34:44.030
If I could. I would.

605
00:34:44.040 --> 00:34:46.580
But it appears they have a psychic barrier to my abilities.

606
00:34:47.080 --> 00:34:48.500
I cannot sense them.

607
00:34:48.500 --> 00:34:50.790
Impressive. Like their genetic coding.

608
00:34:51.210 --> 00:34:54.050
No doubt another evolution in order to hunt undetected.

609
00:34:54.050 --> 00:34:55.130
Impressive?

610
00:34:55.960 --> 00:34:57.670
You think this is impressive?

611
00:34:59.510 --> 00:35:00.840
It was merely an observation.

612
00:35:00.840 --> 00:35:04.060
He killed Duke right in front of you. Spock.

613
00:35:04.060 --> 00:35:07.140
Doesn't that hit you. somewhere deep inside?

614
00:35:07.140 --> 00:35:09.020
No? Nothing?

615
00:35:09.020 --> 00:35:10.850
We just need to reboot navigation.

616
00:35:10.850 --> 00:35:12.310
Can you feel anything?

617
00:35:12.310 --> 00:35:14.770
Or are you just some heartless. pointy-eared computer?

618
00:35:14.780 --> 00:35:15.780
Hey!

619
00:35:19.070 --> 00:35:20.390
Now that that's out of the way...

620
00:35:20.870 --> 00:35:22.200
if we want get out alive...

621
00:35:22.200 --> 00:35:24.950
we have to stop yelling at each other and start listening.

622
00:35:24.950 --> 00:35:26.040
Hemmer.

623
00:35:26.040 --> 00:35:27.830
What is it you're trying to tell us about the nav-comm?

624
00:35:27.830 --> 00:35:29.330
It's the only system left to reboot.

625
00:35:29.330 --> 00:35:30.750
Everything else is online.

626
00:35:30.750 --> 00:35:32.420
That means our mission is complete.

627
00:35:32.920 --> 00:35:34.130
That would be correct.

628
00:35:34.130 --> 00:35:36.590
Okay. Now let's get rid of these Gorn.

629
00:35:36.590 --> 00:35:38.220
La'An. tactical analysis.

630
00:35:38.590 --> 00:35:40.840
The hatchlings have begun molting...

631
00:35:40.840 --> 00:35:43.050
but they aren't fully mature.

632
00:35:43.050 --> 00:35:45.260
At this stage. younglings have an intense drive...

633
00:35:45.260 --> 00:35:47.060
for alpha dominance.

634
00:35:47.060 --> 00:35:50.400
The 2 left will be the strongest. the smartest...

635
00:35:50.400 --> 00:35:52.480
and extremely hostile to each other.

636
00:35:52.480 --> 00:35:53.520
That's a weak spot.

637
00:35:54.270 --> 00:35:56.030
We can work together. that's our advantage.

638
00:35:56.030 --> 00:35:57.670
No matter what. we have to kill them now.

639
00:35:58.280 --> 00:36:00.570
We'd have no chance even against 1 adult Gorn.

640
00:36:00.570 --> 00:36:03.160
These younglings move too fast for us to hunt.

641
00:36:03.160 --> 00:36:05.240
We'll have to create a choke point.

642
00:36:05.240 --> 00:36:08.120
The Gorn are highly intelligent. even at this stage.

643
00:36:08.120 --> 00:36:10.370
A simple trap won't work.

644
00:36:10.370 --> 00:36:12.250
How are we supposed to hunt them?

645
00:36:12.250 --> 00:36:14.250
We can't even track them with sensors.

646
00:36:14.250 --> 00:36:16.000
We make them come to us.

647
00:36:16.920 --> 00:36:19.050
That is very logical.

648
00:36:19.470 --> 00:36:21.930
LA'AN: Gorn can't resist aggressive behavior.

649
00:36:21.930 --> 00:36:23.930
They won't back down from a challenge...

650
00:36:23.930 --> 00:36:26.140
so we can use that to draw them out. put them down.

651
00:36:26.680 --> 00:36:28.430
Great. Now we're bait.

652
00:36:28.440 --> 00:36:30.160
LA'AN: We can use the environment controls.

653
00:36:31.060 --> 00:36:32.610
Gorn avoid the cold.

654
00:36:34.230 --> 00:36:36.190
We can force them into the areas we want them in.

655
00:36:36.900 --> 00:36:38.990
Now. this sounds like the start of a plan.

656
00:36:39.450 --> 00:36:40.570
All right.

657
00:36:41.530 --> 00:36:42.570
Let's get to work.

658
00:36:49.370 --> 00:36:51.040
[SPARKS CRACKLING]

659
00:36:59.050 --> 00:37:00.680
[POWERING UP]

660
00:37:00.680 --> 00:37:01.680
Computer...

661
00:37:02.510 --> 00:37:04.760
transfer all functions to comms station.

662
00:37:06.020 --> 00:37:07.720
Captain Pike...

663
00:37:07.730 --> 00:37:10.020
command code 2-4-6-8-10.

664
00:37:10.690 --> 00:37:12.020
You still haven't changed that?

665
00:37:14.650 --> 00:37:16.610
PIKE: <i>We can quarterback the operation from here.</i>

666
00:37:19.030 --> 00:37:20.530
COMPUTER: <i>Temperature decreasing.</i>

667
00:37:22.410 --> 00:37:25.290
As the ship cools. this bay will become a warm oasis for them.

668
00:37:26.660 --> 00:37:28.410
You are okay with what you must do?

669
00:37:29.370 --> 00:37:31.460
If it succeeds. you and I will be trapped in here...

670
00:37:31.460 --> 00:37:32.460
with angry Gorn.

671
00:37:33.210 --> 00:37:34.610
I will not be the one to kill it...

672
00:37:35.210 --> 00:37:37.710
but I will do what I must to protect the lives of this crew.

673
00:37:42.890 --> 00:37:44.720
Hey. Are you okay?

674
00:37:45.560 --> 00:37:47.770
Trust me. there's nothing I'd rather be doing right now...

675
00:37:47.770 --> 00:37:49.270
than fighting back against the Gorn.

676
00:37:52.400 --> 00:37:53.520
UHURA: Game on.

677
00:37:53.520 --> 00:37:55.530
[CLATTERING]

678
00:37:55.940 --> 00:38:00.280
[GROWLING. CLUCKING]

679
00:38:08.910 --> 00:38:09.910
It's here.

680
00:38:10.500 --> 00:38:12.040
[CLUCKING]

681
00:38:12.040 --> 00:38:13.500
[SHRIEKS]

682
00:38:15.090 --> 00:38:16.420
We got one in the chute!

683
00:38:16.420 --> 00:38:21.090
[SHRIEKING. CLUCKING]

684
00:38:26.270 --> 00:38:28.980
Uhura. I'm blasting the Transporter Room now.

685
00:38:29.730 --> 00:38:30.730
Go!

686
00:38:32.860 --> 00:38:33.860
Come on. come on.

687
00:38:34.690 --> 00:38:36.020
[PANTING]

688
00:38:37.190 --> 00:38:38.570
You really are good at everything.

689
00:38:40.820 --> 00:38:42.950
[CLUCKING]

690
00:38:42.950 --> 00:38:45.510
PIKE: <i>It's going into the vent system. Spock. get into position.</i>

691
00:38:47.370 --> 00:38:48.870
[WEAPON POWERS UP]

692
00:38:50.790 --> 00:38:52.290
[DISTANT GROWLING]

693
00:38:56.710 --> 00:38:58.460
[DISTANT GROWLING]

694
00:38:58.460 --> 00:39:00.170
[FEET CLATTERING]

695
00:39:00.170 --> 00:39:01.970
[LOW CLUCKING]

696
00:39:01.970 --> 00:39:02.970
It's not responding.

697
00:39:03.760 --> 00:39:04.890
PIKE: <i>You have to draw it out.</i>

698
00:39:04.890 --> 00:39:06.510
LA'AN: <i>Fight it. Spock! Make it angry!</i>

699
00:39:08.140 --> 00:39:10.930
[SCREAMING]

700
00:39:10.940 --> 00:39:12.650
The rage that is in my thoughts...

701
00:39:15.480 --> 00:39:16.650
I let into my heart.

702
00:39:18.480 --> 00:39:21.490
[SHOUTING]

703
00:39:23.370 --> 00:39:24.950
[CLUCKING]
- [GRUNTS]

704
00:39:24.950 --> 00:39:25.990
[GORN CHITTERS]

705
00:39:29.080 --> 00:39:32.330
[GORN CHITTERING]

706
00:39:32.330 --> 00:39:34.450
PIKE: <i>Why does my audio sound like there are 2 Gorn?</i>

707
00:39:35.340 --> 00:39:37.670
The other one is here. It's boxing him in.

708
00:39:37.670 --> 00:39:39.510
PIKE: <i>Spock. watch for the 2ⁿᵈ Gorn.</i>

709
00:39:39.510 --> 00:39:40.510
[GORN SHRIEKS]

710
00:39:41.840 --> 00:39:43.010
[SHRIEKS]

711
00:39:44.260 --> 00:39:46.470
Hey. hey. easy. easy. It's me. It's me.

712
00:39:46.470 --> 00:39:47.810
[POUNDING ON DOOR]

713
00:39:52.060 --> 00:39:54.860
[GORN SHRIEKING IN DISTANCE]

714
00:39:59.650 --> 00:40:00.990
SAM: They've turned on each other.

715
00:40:00.990 --> 00:40:02.990
[SHRIEKING CONTINUES]

716
00:40:10.710 --> 00:40:12.630
When those 2 are finished there'll be 1 left.

717
00:40:14.210 --> 00:40:15.630
The alpha.

718
00:40:15.630 --> 00:40:17.170
We put that down. we go home.

719
00:40:20.470 --> 00:40:21.970
[WEAPON POWERS UP]

720
00:40:22.970 --> 00:40:24.100
Hemmer...

721
00:40:24.640 --> 00:40:25.890
<i>I'm coming your way.</i>

722
00:40:36.770 --> 00:40:40.440
[LOW GROWLING. CLUCKING]

723
00:40:42.990 --> 00:40:44.070
Come on!

724
00:40:51.290 --> 00:40:52.290
[CLATTERS]

725
00:40:53.670 --> 00:40:55.000
I'm unarmed.

726
00:40:55.000 --> 00:40:56.920
It's just you and me.

727
00:40:58.090 --> 00:41:00.590
Fight me! Come on. fight me!

728
00:41:01.970 --> 00:41:03.470
[ROARS]

729
00:41:04.760 --> 00:41:06.760
[GROWLING]

730
00:41:08.770 --> 00:41:10.770
[SHRIEKS]

731
00:41:18.940 --> 00:41:21.780
[SHRIEKING]

732
00:41:35.420 --> 00:41:37.170
Hemmer. now! Do it now!

733
00:41:40.760 --> 00:41:43.260
[SHRIEKING]

734
00:41:56.640 --> 00:41:58.690
♪♪

735
00:42:24.220 --> 00:42:26.390
[SHOUTING]

736
00:42:30.350 --> 00:42:31.350
[EXHALES]

737
00:42:33.650 --> 00:42:34.900
It's dead. Chris.

738
00:42:36.020 --> 00:42:37.020
Yeah?

739
00:42:38.400 --> 00:42:40.070
[GRUNTING]

740
00:42:48.700 --> 00:42:50.660
We did it. That's the last of them.

741
00:42:52.620 --> 00:42:53.620
Not quite.

742
00:42:55.330 --> 00:42:56.630
I'm going to go outside now.

743
00:43:00.010 --> 00:43:01.720
[GROANING]

744
00:43:03.050 --> 00:43:04.340
Hemmer. what's going on?

745
00:43:04.340 --> 00:43:05.760
I may not be able to sense them...

746
00:43:05.760 --> 00:43:08.510
but I know my own body very well.

747
00:43:08.930 --> 00:43:11.270
The spray. It's more than a venom.

748
00:43:12.270 --> 00:43:13.560
It's how they reproduce.

749
00:43:14.730 --> 00:43:15.810
Captain. open the door.

750
00:43:16.980 --> 00:43:18.070
PIKE: I... I can't.

751
00:43:18.900 --> 00:43:20.610
I do not want anyone to try to stop me.

752
00:43:20.990 --> 00:43:22.280
We can extract them.

753
00:43:24.320 --> 00:43:26.570
We'll neutralize the growth process...

754
00:43:26.580 --> 00:43:27.700
figure something out.

755
00:43:28.370 --> 00:43:30.500
If we had more time. I'm sure you could.

756
00:43:31.080 --> 00:43:32.750
But it's too late to... [GROANS]

757
00:43:34.830 --> 00:43:36.210
We all know what's coming.

758
00:43:36.210 --> 00:43:37.590
Hemmer. you don't have to do this.

759
00:43:38.420 --> 00:43:39.420
<i>But. Captain...</i>

760
00:43:40.590 --> 00:43:41.880
<i>my sacrifice...</i>

761
00:43:41.880 --> 00:43:44.130
will save the lives of those I care most about.

762
00:43:45.800 --> 00:43:47.430
For me. there is no other choice.

763
00:43:48.260 --> 00:43:49.510
[GROANS]

764
00:43:49.510 --> 00:43:50.600
A logical conclusion.

765
00:43:54.020 --> 00:43:57.110
Live long and prosper. my friend.

766
00:44:01.990 --> 00:44:04.280
No. No! We can help you. [POUNDS ON DOOR]

767
00:44:04.280 --> 00:44:05.660
You have to let us try.

768
00:44:06.450 --> 00:44:08.450
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY] Uhura.

769
00:44:11.080 --> 00:44:13.790
I want to leave you with 1 last piece of advice.

770
00:44:15.250 --> 00:44:16.330
Open yourself.

771
00:44:17.920 --> 00:44:20.000
Make a home for yourself amongst others...

772
00:44:20.000 --> 00:44:23.630
and you will find joy more often than sadness.

773
00:44:26.800 --> 00:44:27.800
Hemmer.

774
00:44:28.930 --> 00:44:30.850
[VOICE BREAKING] Hemmer. please. please...

775
00:44:33.440 --> 00:44:34.810
HEMMER: <i>Do not weep for me.</i>

776
00:44:34.810 --> 00:44:36.480
[SOBBING]

777
00:44:38.480 --> 00:44:39.690
I've had a good life.

778
00:44:42.150 --> 00:44:43.320
[WINCES]

779
00:44:45.660 --> 00:44:46.820
It's time for me to go.

780
00:44:49.820 --> 00:44:52.080
♪♪

781
00:44:53.750 --> 00:44:55.750
[UHURA CONTINUES SOBBING]

782
00:45:06.090 --> 00:45:08.100
[GRUNTING]

783
00:45:19.360 --> 00:45:20.440
[GRUNTS SOFTLY]

784
00:45:21.360 --> 00:45:23.030
Just like Andoria.

785
00:45:27.200 --> 00:45:28.530
[SQUELCHING]

786
00:45:43.610 --> 00:45:45.660
♪♪

787
00:46:13.710 --> 00:46:16.870
ORTEGAS: This sucks. I hate funerals.

788
00:46:16.880 --> 00:46:19.630
But if Hemmer was here. he would remind us...

789
00:46:19.630 --> 00:46:21.130
that this is a celebration.

790
00:46:22.170 --> 00:46:25.760
"Exalt the fallen and commit them to the cosmos."

791
00:46:26.890 --> 00:46:29.410
Then he would have scolded me for pushing the engines too hard.

792
00:46:30.100 --> 00:46:31.780
And I would have called him a Blue Meanie.

793
00:46:32.640 --> 00:46:33.770
And we'd laugh.

794
00:46:38.190 --> 00:46:39.860
And it wouldn't have felt like a funeral.

795
00:46:47.030 --> 00:46:49.660
Best engineer I have ever served with.

796
00:46:52.160 --> 00:46:53.580
UHURA: I never told Hemmer...

797
00:46:53.580 --> 00:46:56.250
but he reminded me a lot of my dad.

798
00:46:57.790 --> 00:47:00.630
Always pushing me to see things from a new perspective.

799
00:47:01.510 --> 00:47:03.510
Do better. be better.

800
00:47:05.510 --> 00:47:06.800
Losing Hemmer...

801
00:47:07.970 --> 00:47:08.970
hurts.

802
00:47:13.020 --> 00:47:16.560
The people you love the most can cause you the most pain.

803
00:47:19.230 --> 00:47:21.610
But it's the people you love that can mend your heart...

804
00:47:21.610 --> 00:47:22.940
when you feel broken.

805
00:47:25.570 --> 00:47:27.320
That's what Hemmer's purpose was.

806
00:47:28.990 --> 00:47:30.990
To fix what is broken.

807
00:47:34.580 --> 00:47:35.620
And he did.

808
00:47:46.470 --> 00:47:47.800
[DOOR WHOOSHES OPEN]

809
00:47:57.230 --> 00:47:58.440
CHAPEL: Spock.

810
00:48:00.150 --> 00:48:01.230
Do not follow me.

811
00:48:02.280 --> 00:48:04.360
What's going on?
- I'm warning you. back off!

812
00:48:14.790 --> 00:48:16.370
Tell me what's going on.

813
00:48:18.210 --> 00:48:19.290
I can't control it.

814
00:48:21.090 --> 00:48:22.590
I've let something out.

815
00:48:22.590 --> 00:48:23.840
Rage. Pain.

816
00:48:26.880 --> 00:48:28.010
It's your emotions.

817
00:48:30.560 --> 00:48:31.720
My mind has gotten weak.

818
00:48:31.720 --> 00:48:32.720
No. no.

819
00:48:34.350 --> 00:48:36.770
It doesn't make you weak. Spock.

820
00:48:37.560 --> 00:48:38.810
It makes you human.

821
00:48:58.280 --> 00:49:00.330
♪♪

822
00:49:19.610 --> 00:49:21.520
So. I found the lead...

823
00:49:21.520 --> 00:49:23.150
on Oriana's family.

824
00:49:26.070 --> 00:49:27.790
Someone out there might be looking for her.

825
00:49:28.490 --> 00:49:29.490
How strong of a lead?

826
00:49:31.740 --> 00:49:33.240
Not very.

827
00:49:33.250 --> 00:49:34.790
It's. uh. weak. actually.

828
00:49:35.620 --> 00:49:37.420
And it's outside Federation space.

829
00:49:38.120 --> 00:49:39.670
But you want to pursue it anyway?

830
00:49:42.000 --> 00:49:43.630
I know what it feels like to be alone.

831
00:49:43.630 --> 00:49:46.300
If there's any chance she still has people out there...

832
00:49:46.300 --> 00:49:47.470
A mission like this...

833
00:49:49.340 --> 00:49:50.550
it takes time.

834
00:49:52.970 --> 00:49:55.020
I'd like to request a formal leave of absence.

835
00:49:56.940 --> 00:49:58.480
Decommission me if you have to...

836
00:49:58.480 --> 00:50:01.150
but I need the freedom to go where the clues take me.

837
00:50:03.610 --> 00:50:05.440
If I said no. would it make a difference?

838
00:50:07.320 --> 00:50:08.660
I...

839
00:50:08.660 --> 00:50:09.860
I'll square it with Starfleet.

840
00:50:10.530 --> 00:50:11.580
Whatever you need.

841
00:50:12.330 --> 00:50:13.330
But. La'An...

842
00:50:14.790 --> 00:50:15.910
however long it takes...

843
00:50:17.830 --> 00:50:19.000
come back to us. okay?

844
00:50:20.920 --> 00:50:22.040
Aye. sir.

845
00:50:32.310 --> 00:50:33.310
Captain.

846
00:50:37.350 --> 00:50:38.350
Chris.

847
00:50:40.940 --> 00:50:41.940
Thank you.

848
00:50:44.280 --> 00:50:45.440
For everything.

849
00:51:01.970 --> 00:51:04.020
♪♪

850
00:51:17.810 --> 00:51:19.150
[CONSOLE BEEPING SOFTLY]

851
00:51:31.510 --> 00:52:43.050
%$%$

852
00:51:34.510 --> 00:52:43.050
STAR TREK

853
00:51:34.510 --> 00:52:43.050
STRANGE NEW WORLDS
